      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, College of Education (Behavior Analysis Program)",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-06-26\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWelcome to Career Opportunities at Lindenwood University. PLEASE READ: For all applications, please include your resume and cover letter. You may skip the “ Quick Apply ” page by simply clicking “ Next ” at the bottom of the page. When you arrive at the “ Experience ” page, you may upload all desired documents using the upload box labeled “ Resume/CV. ” This is the appropriate box to upload all documents. JOB TITLE SUMMARY Job title: Adjunct Instructor, School of Education (Behavior Analysis Program) Job code: Varies           Department: School of Education Evaluation group: Adjunct Instructor FLSA status: Exempt             Grade: Varies                 Reports to: Varies        Positions supervised: N/A     Notice: At this time, we may not be actively recruiting for positions in this/these area(s). Applications submitted will be added to a pool of candidates to be considered for future openings. Summary Adjunct instructors are responsible for teaching and related administrative activities.  This position may also include academic advising, program design, and student mentoring. Position will teach courses within the Master of Arts in Behavior Analysis Program. Candidate must have 1-2 experience in the practical application of the various research designs used in ABA as well as the various dimensions of measurement.  Candidate must hold certification in Behavior Analysis. Must have the ability to teach and ensure proof of learning of the various concepts and skills on the BACB Fourth Edition Task List Sections A and B. Proof of learning would include fluency of terms and application concepts. Essential Job Functions and Performance Indicators Teaching and Learning Focus on the talents, interests, and future of the student by clearly communicating learning goals and how those goals are assessed, teaching course sessions in an organized way, providing time for reflection, discuss